<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.10.6: Writing Inequalities to Represent a Situation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00553</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.10.6: Writing Inequalities to Represent a Situation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>802d7340-9a07-432f-8d34-b3752f3535c3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <para id="para-00001">Use the following scenerio for questions 1 - 2.</para>
      <para id="para-00002"><quote id="quote-00001">Lin’s job pays $8.25 an hour plus $10 of transportation allowance each week. She
        has to work at least 5 hours a week to keep the job, and she can earn up to $175 per week,
        including $10 to cover transportation per week.</quote></para>

      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Represent this situation mathematically. If you use variables, specify what each one
            means.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>

          <para id="para-00005">\(8.25h\;+\;10\;\leq\;175\) and \(h\;\geq\;5\), where \(h\) represents the number of
            hours Lin works in a week.</para>

        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">How many hours per week can Lin work? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is an example.</para>

          <para id="para-00008">At least 5 hours and at most 20 hours (or \(5\leq\;h\;\leq20\)). For example: The
            maximum amount she could earn, not including the transportation allowance, is $165. That
            amount is equal to 20 hours of work, \(\frac{165}{8.25}=20\)."</para>

        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>
  </content>
